  "rendered_prompt": "<|system|>You are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|end|><|user|>Paragraph:\n\"\"\"\nHamlet is a character who thinks too much and acts too little. After his father's ghost tells him that Claudius murdered him, Hamlet promises to get revenge. But instead of acting right away, he spends most of the play doubting himself and planning. In his famous speech, he asks, \"To be, or not to be,\" as he wonders whether life is worth the pain. Even when he has a perfect chance to kill Claudius while he is praying, he decides to wait. His delay ends up causing the deaths of many people, including himself.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer selected this text:\n\"\"\"\nIn his famous speech, he asks, \"To be, or not to be,\" as he wonders whether life is worth the pain.\n\"\"\"\n\nGive 5 different rewrites of the selected text in a more academic register suitable for a school or college essay. Keep the same meaning and the same level of certainty. Do not add evidence, statistics, names, citations or new ideas. Put the best options first.<|end|><|assistant|>",
